# CRLF must survive clone/checkout.
#
# assets/dsh-tools.bat is parsed by cmd.exe, which silently truncates an
# LF-only batch file at a `call :LABEL` boundary — the scheduler dies with no
# error. Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` would store it as LF and break
# every clone, so the batch file is pinned to CRLF in the repository itself.
#
# Do not relax this. Verify after a fresh clone with:
#   node scripts/check-crlf.js
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# PowerShell and JS tolerate LF, but keeping them explicit avoids per-machine
# churn in diffs.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.js  text eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets
*.tgz binary
